      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just figured I'd report that this is still an issue as of current. Only finally noticed it because of a particularly high-bloom world I was visiting and it kept resetting on rejoin.\n\nI understand why you may not want it to persist by default because many people will lower it as a one-time choice and then forget about it, so I think a checkbox for persistence makes sense.\n\nBut at the very least if there isn't going to be persistence then the bloom slider should reflect that and go back to 100% on world change as to not confuse people. Perhaps a bit of text above or below the slider informing the user that the setting is not persistent would be called for.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
